Feature: Vertical take-off and landing
  A VTOL needs no runway and no throw. You arm it, and VTOL TKOF lifts it straight up to the
  plan altitude. It stays there until you tell it to do something else. QLAND brings it
  straight down, and ArduPilot disarms it when it is on the ground.

  Expectation: VTOL TKOF lifts the plane straight up
    Given the vehicle is armed
    And the plane is on the ground
    When the operator takes off vertically
    Then the flight is hovering
    And the height above home is at least 15 m

  Expectation: QLAND brings the plane straight down
    Given the flight is hovering
    When the operator lands vertically
    Then the plane is on the ground
    And the vehicle is disarmed
